# Homepage speed

The brand catalogues are hundreds of MB. Any static import chain from a route
to `@/data/products` bundles them into that route's chunk, and every cold
instance parses it (~9s). Per-request catalogue work made `/` take ~15s
(Sep 2026 incident).

- `/` gets product cards from `getHomepageData()` in `src/lib/homepage-feed.ts`,
  which fetches `/api/home-data?v=<deployment>` (CDN + Next Data Cache, 1h).
  Only `app/api/home-data/route.ts` statically imports `src/lib/homepage-data.ts`
  (the heavy builder). `homepage-feed.ts` may only type-import it plus the
  dynamic-import fallback.
- Never import `@/data/products`, `@/lib/homepage-data` or `@/lib/cart-server`
  from `app/layout.tsx`, `app/page.tsx` or anything they render. The layout
  reads the cart badge via `@/lib/cart-count` (cookie only).
- New homepage sections: add fields to `HomepageData` / `buildHomepageData`,
  read them via `getHomepageData()`. Cache card fields only
  (`toProductCardProduct`) — Data Cache items are capped at 2MB.
- Functions run in `icn1` (Seoul, `vercel.json` `regions`) — customers are in
  Korea; do not remove.
- `.github/workflows/homepage-speed-guard.yml` pings `/` every 10 min (keeps
  it warm) and fails if TTFB > 8s. A failing run means a regression — fix it.
- Ship homepage/layout changes via a preview branch first
  (`scripts/ship-*.sh` pattern): a failed build on `main` blocks all deploys,
  including catalogue syncs.
- Tried and failed: static layout + ISR (Vercel build failed at prerender,
  log not captured); `await import()` inside `unstable_cache` callbacks (every
  request recomputed).
